hing input order.')\nadd('Does the two-paragraph condition use a logical conjunction?', False, 'current_code.py line 193 uses a bitwise & within chained comparisons; the revision uses len(paragraphs) == 2.')\nadd('Does the LightGBM configuration also request balanced class weights?', True, 'current_code.py line 1123 sets class_weight=\\\"balanced\\\" after synthetic balancing.')\nadd('Are custom-objective target moments fixed constants?', True, 'current_code.py lines 902-903 set a=2.998 and b=1.092; the revision derives moments from the actual unresampled labels.')\nadd('Can the row identity of the external OOF ndarray be independently verified here?', False, 'current_code.py loads oof.pkl as a six-column array without IDs; competition artifacts are unavailable. The existing train.csv ordering assumption is retained explicitly.')\nadd('Does the task note a training-to-test source shift?', True, 'task.md summary says the test resembles non-Persuade data; no source labels are available locally, so calibration shifts are bounded and cross-checked.')\nreport = dict(observations=obs, action_summary='Remove pre-CV topic downsampling, SMOTE, mean imputation, and inverse-class weighting to restore the natural training distribution after the documented regression. Repair floating-point OOF storage and identifier alignment; generate live test features instead of merging a static public-test cache, retaining only reproducible ranked features and transformer stacking outputs. Keep the established LightGBM ensemble, derive QWK objective moments from the real labels, and adopt bounded ordinal cutpoints only when cross-fitted calibration improves QWK. No training or inference was run; leaderboard improvement remains unmeasured.')\nPath('output/report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\nPY\npython output/rewrite.py\npython -m py_compile output/revised_code.py\"","aggregated_output":"output/revised_code.py:170: SyntaxWarning: invalid escape sequence '\\w'\n  x = re.sub(